{#
  name: _shell (helper, not a section)
  purpose: The section skeleton every section uses (R-SEC-01, R-SEC-06, R-SEC-10, R-TOK-15, R-LAY-02): padding by density, surface, container, eyebrow + h2 + lede, body via caller, optional CTA, entrances below the fold (R-MOT-05).
  usage: {% call shell("feature-grid", s, ctx) %} …body… {% endcall %}; opts: itemsReveal (items carry their own entrances; the heading group arrives on its own and the section clips horizontal overflow because items may slide), clipX (overflow-x-clip for sliding rows), noReveal, center (true centres the heading group; the default is start-aligned, DESIGN §4), kind ("scale" for a framed object; the default rise), extra (classes appended to the section, e.g. a depth backdrop)
  ctx: { locale, pageUrl, density, surface, reveal, index, flair }; flair = the booleans of the brief's motion level (R-TOK-12): vocabulary, pop, rule, …
  macros: enter (one entrance: from-state + transition + delay), revealClasses (section entrance), headingClasses (heading group), item (grid item: treatment and delay by column, R-MOT-16), stagger (list item: delay by index), pop (icon pop), zoom (picture settle), depth (R-MOT-15), eyebrowRule (the marker that draws). Below the standard level (no flair.vocabulary) every kind falls back to a rise: calm is rise only (R-TOK-12).
  how entrances work (R-MOT-05, R-MOT-10): an element carrying `pending:` utilities waits in its from-state (faded and offset) until enhance.js marks it data-revealed when its top crosses 88 % of the viewport height, then transitions to its final state over --reveal-duration on --ease-reveal after its delay. The transition utilities sit under data-revealed: so they exist only for the entrance itself: entering the from-state when the script starts is instant, never a fade-out. Time-based, once, independent of scroll speed. `pending:` exists only on screen, with JS and with motion allowed, so without any of those the page shows final states; elements already in view at load are marked before `pending:` can apply, so nothing above the fold animates (R-MOT-11).
#}
{% from "primitives/button.njk" import button with context %}
{#- One entrance: kind "" rise | "start" slide in from the inline start | "end" from the inline end | "settle" rise and grow from 94 % | "scale" grow from 96 %; delay in ms. -#}
{% macro enter(kind="", delay=0) %}{% if flair and not flair.vocabulary %}{% set kind = "" %}{% endif %} pending:opacity-0{% if kind == "start" %} pending:-translate-x-(--reveal-distance) rtl:pending:translate-x-(--reveal-distance){% elif kind == "end" %} pending:translate-x-(--reveal-distance) rtl:pending:-translate-x-(--reveal-distance){% elif kind == "scale" %} pending:scale-96{% else %} pending:translate-y-(--reveal-distance){% if kind == "settle" %} pending:scale-94{% endif %}{% endif %} motion-safe:data-revealed:transition-[opacity,translate,scale] motion-safe:data-revealed:duration-(--reveal-duration) motion-safe:data-revealed:ease-reveal{% if delay %} motion-safe:data-revealed:delay-{{ delay }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Section entrance (sections that arrive as one, media rows, the CTA panel). sdaOnly is kept for callers and ignored. -#}
{% macro revealClasses(on, kind="", sdaOnly=false) %}{% if on %}{{ enter(kind) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Heading group of a section whose items arrive on their own: rises first. -#}
{% macro headingClasses(on) %}{% if on %}{{ enter() }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Column delay: items in one row cross the trigger line together and cascade 90 ms apart; the next row starts over (R-MOT-16). -#}
{% macro colDelay(i, cols) %}{{ (i % cols) * 90 }}{% endmacro %}
{#- Grid item (R-MOT-16): the treatment of the item's column (3 columns: slide-in / rise / framed settle; 4: + slide-from-end; 2: slide-in / slide-from-end) and its column delay; kind forces one treatment ("rise", "start", "end", "settle", "scale"). -#}
{% macro item(i, cols, ctx, kind="") %}{% if ctx.reveal %}{% set c = i % cols %}{% set t = kind %}{% if not t and ctx.flair and ctx.flair.vocabulary %}{% set v = ["start", "rise", "settle", "end"] if cols == 4 else (["start", "end"] if cols == 2 else ["start", "rise", "settle"]) %}{% set t = v[c] %}{% endif %}{{ enter("" if t == "rise" else t, c * 90) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- List item (logo cloud, timeline, steps, awards): 70 ms after the previous, eight at most (R-MOT-03). -#}
{% macro stagger(i, kind="") %}{% if i < 8 %}{{ enter("" if kind == "rise" else kind, i * 70) }}{% else %}{{ enter("" if kind == "rise" else kind, 490) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Icon pop (expressive): the icon tile, avatar or badge grows from 70 % with a slight overshoot (--ease-spring), 180 ms after its item starts. -#}
{% macro pop(ctx, delay=0) %}{% if ctx.reveal and ctx.flair and ctx.flair.pop %} pending:scale-70 pending:opacity-0 motion-safe:data-revealed:transition-[opacity,scale] motion-safe:data-revealed:duration-(--reveal-duration) motion-safe:data-revealed:ease-spring motion-safe:data-revealed:delay-{{ delay + 180 }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Picture settle (standard): the picture inside its clipped frame eases from 115 % to its resting scale as it enters. -#}
{% macro zoom(ctx) %}{% if ctx.reveal and ctx.flair and ctx.flair.vocabulary %} pending:scale-115 motion-safe:data-revealed:transition-[scale] motion-safe:data-revealed:duration-1200 motion-safe:data-revealed:ease-reveal{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Depth (R-MOT-15): a decorative layer moves on scroll() or on its own view(), md and up, linear; drift mirrors under rtl:. pseudo = "before:" puts it on a pseudo-element. Callers gate on ctx.flair. Depth is the one thing that stays tied to the scroll: it is meant to track it. -#}
{% macro depth(kind, timeline="view()", range="cover_0%_cover_100%", pseudo="") %} md:motion-safe:sda:{{ pseudo }}animate-{{ kind }}{% if kind == "drift" %} rtl:md:motion-safe:sda:{{ pseudo }}animate-drift-end{% endif %} md:motion-safe:sda:{{ pseudo }}[animation-timeline:{{ timeline }}] md:motion-safe:sda:{{ pseudo }}[animation-range:{{ range }}]{% endmacro %}
{#- The eyebrow marker (DESIGN §4): a 24 px accent rule before the label that draws from the start edge 200 ms after its heading group starts to rise. -#}
{% macro eyebrowRule(inverse=false, draw=false) %}before:h-0.5 before:w-6 before:rounded-full {{ 'before:bg-ink-inverse/70' if inverse else 'before:bg-accent-600' }}{% if draw %} before:origin-left rtl:before:origin-right pending:before:scale-x-0 motion-safe:data-revealed:before:transition-transform motion-safe:data-revealed:before:duration-(--reveal-duration) motion-safe:data-revealed:before:ease-reveal motion-safe:data-revealed:before:delay-200{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro shell(name, s, ctx, opts={}) %}
{%- set pad = "py-12 md:py-16" if ctx.density == "compact" else "py-16 md:py-24" -%}
{%- set surface = s.surface or ctx.surface or "bg-surface" -%}
{%- set inverse = surface == "bg-brand-700" -%}
{%- set reveal = ctx.reveal and not opts.noReveal -%}
{%- set center = opts.center === true -%}
<section class="{{ pad }} {{ surface }}{% if inverse %} text-ink-inverse{% endif %}{% if opts.clipX or (opts.itemsReveal and reveal) %} overflow-x-clip{% endif %}{% if opts.extra %} {{ opts.extra }}{% endif %}{% if not opts.itemsReveal %}{{ revealClasses(reveal, opts.kind) }}{% endif %}" data-component="{{ name }}"{% if s.variant %} data-variant="{{ s.variant }}"{% endif %}{% if s.anchor %} id="{{ s.anchor }}"{% endif %}{% if not s.title and s.label %} aria-label="{{ s.label }}"{% endif %}>
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
{%- if s.title or s.eyebrow or s.lede %}
{%- set hg = "hgroup" if s.title else "div" %}
<{{ hg }} class="{{ 'mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center' if center else 'max-w-3xl' }}{{ headingClasses(reveal and opts.itemsReveal) }}">
{%- if s.eyebrow %}<p class="flex items-center gap-2 {{ 'justify-center' if center }} text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide {{ 'text-ink-inverse/80' if inverse else 'text-ink-brand' }} {{ eyebrowRule(inverse, reveal and ctx.flair and ctx.flair.rule) }}">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
{%- if s.title %}<h2 class="{{ 'mt-2' if s.eyebrow }} text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">{{ s.title | wbr | safe }}</h2>{% endif %}
{%- if s.lede %}<p class="mt-4 text-lg md:text-xl {{ 'text-ink-inverse/80' if inverse else 'text-ink-muted' }}">{{ s.lede }}</p>{% endif %}
</{{ hg }}>
{%- endif %}
<div class="{{ 'mt-12 md:mt-16' if (s.title or s.eyebrow or s.lede) }}">
{{ caller() }}
</div>
{%- if s.cta %}
<div class="mt-12 {{ 'text-center' if center }}">{{ button(s.cta.label, { href: s.cta.href, variant: s.cta.variant or "secondary", iconEnd: "arrow-right" }) }}</div>
{%- endif %}
</div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
